Snyk (pronounced "sneak") is a developer-security platform that scans your code,
dependencies, containers, and IaC for known vulnerabilities.

Key pieces:

Component                         What it scans

Snyk Open Source                  Vulnerable dependencies (npm, maven, pip, etc.)
Snyk Code                          Static analysis of your own source code (SAST)
Snyk Container                     Docker/OCI images for CVEs in base layers
Snyk IaC                           Terraform, K8s manifests, CloudFormation misconfigs

It integrates into CI/CD (Jenkins, GitHub Actions) and fails builds on policy violations — this is
likely why it's in your Worldpay security stack alongside SonarQube (code quality) and Sysdig
(runtime/container security).

Two-line interview answer: "Snyk is a shift-left security tool that scans code, open-source dependencies, containers, and IaC for vulnerabilities, integrated directly into the CI/CD pipeline to block insecure builds before deployment."

